10639	{"artifactId":"LLD-d6a4bc79bece9d1f-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-d6a4bc79bece9d1f-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-10T15:07:49.617Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the ISSUE's whole fix intent: a per-session lock held until the CLI process has really exited (not just until its stream ends), every turn for the session waits on it, the panel shows that it is waiting, the holder and its children are stopped only after a timeout and its exit is confirmed, and Stop still ends a turn at once.","evidence":"ISSUE.md Fix intent: \"A lock per chat session is held from the moment a CLI process is started ... until that process has actually exited ... A new message, or any other turn for the session, waits ... If the lock is not released within a set timeout, the holding process (and anything it started) is stopped, its exit is confirmed ... Stop still ends the running turn at once.\" The LLD covers each part. The lease is tied to the exit via onSpawn/attach (2.2, 2.4). runTurn acquires it, and every path goes through runTurn: submit-turn, the grant re-run at chat-panel.ts:856/859, and the selection reply at :905. A waiting status is posted. The timeout stops the process group (detached spawn), then the exit is awaited. Stop calls cancelActive without a timeout. The lock file covers other windows, which the ISSUE root cause names: \"neither the panel nor another panel or window can tell\". [files: docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-chat-panel-concurrent-E20261010d6a4bc79/ISSUE.md, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Migration 'State before' and 2.4/3.3 say that today cli-adapter.ts run() kills the child with an unawaited SIGTERM at its first done event, so a process outlives its answer only by ignoring the kill.","evidence":"The kill lives in run()'s `finally { proc.kill(); ... }` at cli-adapter.ts:754-757. That block runs only when the generator finishes or the consumer calls return(). The panel's runTurn reads the iterator by hand and simply `break`s on done (chat-panel.ts:675-681). It never calls iterator.return(). Its finally (:698-703) only clears activeIterator/activeTurnId, so a later cancelActive cannot reach the turn either. The generator stays parked at `yield` on the done event, so in the panel the finally, and the kill, never run after a normal done. That is how the process outlives its answer, unkilled and untracked. The 'kill at the first done' that the design removes does not happen today on the panel path. Only consumers that drive the generator to the end (collect() in the tests) or abandon it with return() reach the kill. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"Correct the State before: the panel abandons the iterator at done without return(), so the child is neither killed nor tracked. Make sure the new lifecycle does not rely on run()'s finally for anything on the done path (for example releasing the lease or clearing pendingByTurn). In the panel path that finally never runs.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The real spawner does not detach the CLI, so only the direct child is signalled.","evidence":"nodeSpawner at cli-adapter.ts:902: `nodeChildSpawn(command, [...args], { cwd: opts.cwd, stdio: ['pipe','pipe','pipe'] })`. There is no `detached` option, and kill is `child.kill('SIGTERM')` (:950-951), which signals only the direct child. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The change sites are complete. The design lists only session-lock.ts, cli-adapter.ts, chat-panel.ts, extension.ts and the adapter test for the waiting state and the new setting.","evidence":"Three needed sites are missing. (1) The setting insrc.chat.turnLockTimeoutMs must be declared under contributes.configuration in vscode-plugin/package.json, where the other insrc.chat.* settings live (package.json:123 enabled, :129 diffView, :143 lockGroup). The design lists only extension.ts. (2) The waiting status cannot be expressed with today's event types. stream-events.ts:51 limits status to `phase: 'thinking' | 'streaming' | 'tool' | 'editing'`. The webview renders a status through markerFor (markers.ts:47/122), and only `if(running&&mkp)` (chat-panel.ts:463). A 'Waiting for the previous turn to finish' state therefore needs changes in stream-events.ts and markers.ts, plus the inline webview script, or a new host-to-webview message. None of these is listed. (3) The webview must keep Stop available while waiting, which again touches the inline script. [files: vscode-plugin/package.json, vscode-plugin/src/chat/stream-events.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/markers.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"Add vscode-plugin/package.json (the setting declaration), stream-events.ts, markers.ts (or a new message type) and the webview script in chat-panel.ts to the change sites, and say how the waiting state is encoded.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Invariant c2 and section 2.4 say run() 'still ends at the first done or error event' and yields the same events as today.","evidence":"Today run() does not end at done when it is pulled further. After yielding done, the inner `break` (cli-adapter.ts:728) only leaves the events loop. The outer `for await (const line of proc.lines())` (:705) then waits for the next stdout line or for stdout to close before `if (sawDone || sawError) break` (:706). It then runs `const { code, signal } = await proc.exit;` (:731) before returning. For a process that outlives its answer, a fully drained run() does not settle until the process exits. The panel only avoids this by abandoning the iterator. The planned test 'run() ends at the first done event without killing the process' would hang against a still-alive fake unless the post-done `await proc.exit` and the next-line wait are removed. The design presents this as preserved behaviour rather than as a change. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"State this as a change: return straight after a terminal event without awaiting proc.exit, and keep pendingByTurn and the live map alive until the exit settles, so in-turn decide() still reaches a live process. Alternatively, keep the panel's abandon-at-done pattern and say so.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing callers and tests of createChatPanelHost keep working without a lock registry, because the new deps are optional with an in-memory default.","evidence":"extension.ts:512 builds the only production host with `createChatPanelHost({...})`. The new sessionLocks and turnLockTimeoutMs are declared optional (`?: ... | undefined`) with an in-memory default, so the existing deps object and the chat-panel test fakes still type-check. StreamAdapter.cancel changing from void to Promise<void> also stays compatible with the only in-repo callers, chat-panel.ts:582 and deriveChatTitle at cli-adapter.ts:857, which call it as a statement. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1–ac5 maps to a test that would fail without the fix.","evidence":"ac5: today collect() drains run(), whose finally calls proc.kill() (cli-adapter.ts:757), so a 'without killing' assertion fails, and onSpawn does not exist. ac1 and ac2: today runTurn starts the next adapter.run at once (chat-panel.ts:596-644), so 'waits until the holder exits' and 'starts after its exit' fail. ac3: no lock file exists today. ac4: there is no waiting turn to cancel today, so the test cannot pass. One gap: no test covers the panel's new-chat, open-chat and dispose paths, which still call cancelActive() (chat-panel.ts:773, 793, 927, 960). The design does not say whether switching chats waits or stops. That is outside the stated ACs. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"Optionally add a test pinning what new-chat/open-chat/dispose do to a running holder under the lock.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":4,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-10T15:07:49.617Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"current-behaviour.1":{"findingId":"current-behaviour.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: State before now says the panel abandons the iterator at done without return(), so run()'s finally never runs and the outliving process is neither killed nor tracked; the new lifecycle chains cleanup on proc.exit, not on the finally.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-10T15:10:06.419Z"},"change-sites.1":{"findingId":"change-sites.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: added package.json (setting declaration), stream-events.ts (status phase 'waiting'), markers.ts (host and webview label) and the inline webview script (Stop stays available while waiting) to the change sites, with how the waiting state is encoded.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-10T15:10:06.421Z"},"preserved-behaviour.1":{"findingId":"preserved-behaviour.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: 2.4 now states as a change that run() returns right after its first terminal event without awaiting proc.exit or killing; the live entry and pending requests live until the exit settles so decide() still works; invariant c2 narrowed to the events yielded.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-10T15:10:06.421Z"}}}}}}
